      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c3b9e71d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: amsterdam_hamster_dam; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes an aerial view of Amsterdam with the text 'amsterdam' and a picture of a hamster with the text 'hamster dam', creating a pun-based joke. The intent is to play on the word 'dam' by replacing it with 'hamster dam', implying a humorous, absurd, or silly association. While the joke is not inherently abusive, hateful, or propagandistic, it could be considered harmful or offensive to some viewers who may find the pun childish, crude, or disrespectful to the city of Amsterdam. The humor relies on a visual pun and wordplay, which may not be universally appreciated or understood, potentially causing mild offense or discomfort in certain contexts. The meme does not target any specific protected group or community with harmful intent, but its humor may be perceived as dismissive or mocking of the city's name and identity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d1fd5b78"
      },
